    {
      "id": "xxh-3-64-bits",
      "name": "XXH3_64bits",
      "category": "xxhash",
      "signature": "XXH3_64bits(Data, Len)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Data",
          "type": "void*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Len",
          "type": "size_t"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "XXH64_hash_t",
      "docs": "XXH3_64bits():\ndefault 64-bit variant, using default secret and default seed of 0.\nIt's the fastest variant."
    },
    {
      "id": "xxh-3-64-bits-with-secret",
      "name": "XXH3_64bits_withSecret",
      "category": "xxhash",
      "signature": "XXH3_64bits_withSecret(Data, Len, Secret, Secret Size)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Data",
          "type": "void*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Len",
          "type": "size_t"
        },
        {
          "name": "Secret",
          "type": "void*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Secret Size",
          "type": "size_t"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "XXH64_hash_t",
      "docs": "XXH3_64bits_withSecret():\nIt's possible to provide any blob of bytes as a \"secret\" to generate the hash.\nThis makes it more difficult for an external actor to prepare an intentional\ncollision.\nThe secret *must* be large enough (>= XXH3_SECRET_SIZE_MIN).\nIt should consist of random bytes.\nAvoid trivial sequences, such as repeating sequences and especially '\\0',\nas this can cancel out itself.\nFailure to respect these conditions will result in a poor quality hash."
    },
    {
      "id": "xxh-3-64-bits-with-seed",
      "name": "XXH3_64bits_withSeed",
      "category": "xxhash",
      "signature": "XXH3_64bits_withSeed(Data, Len, Seed)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Data",
          "type": "void*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Len",
          "type": "size_t"
        },
        {
          "name": "Seed",
          "type": "XXH64_hash_t"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "XXH64_hash_t",
      "docs": "XXH3_64bits_withSeed():\nThis variant generates a custom secret on the fly based on the default\nsecret, altered using the `seed` value.\nWhile this operation is decently fast, note that it's not completely free.\nNote: seed==0 produces the same results as XXH3_64bits()."
    },
